  </xs:simpleType>
  <xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation> A CreateXXXDataType based on selfDefinedBaseObjectInfoGroup is allowed to
			inherit information from their parents. A CreateXXXDataType based on baseObjectInfoGroup
			can't inherit. The schema does not enforce type-based value restrictions or fields that
			are required to be non-inherited; that is done in the validation rules in the registry.
			See the Validation rules document for details. The base metadata for these is based on
			the groups rather than the resolution types because no ID is present in a creation
			request. Rather than referencing bare groups, the schema wraps them in the
			creationFullInfo and creationSelfDefinedInfo types, which produces better class
			structure in the generated Java bindings. </xs:documentation>
  </xs:annotation>
